# Testing Gates

Use this rule only when changing tests, tooling, CI, or verification policy.

## Commands

| Purpose | Command |
|---------|---------|
| Full gate | `python scripts/verify_phase_completion.py` |
| Tests only | `pytest` |
| Python lint | `ruff check .` |
| Web lint | `npm run lint` |
| Types | `mypy src` |
| Format check | `black --check .` |
| Format apply | `black .` |

Verify script order: `pytest` -> `ruff check .` -> `mypy src` -> `black --check .` -> `npm run lint` -> `npm run test` (web) -> packaging check (fail-fast).

## Practice

- Prefer narrow test runs first when iterating (`pytest path::test_name`).
- Prefer editing existing tests when behavior changes.
- New test files require explicit user authorization; see [test-governance.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/test-governance.mdc) and [agent-testing-policy.md](mdc:docs/agent-testing-policy.md).
- Do not delete tests only to save time.
- Report exact command, pass/fail status, and runtime when claiming results.
- If `black .` modifies files, report format changes separately from test results.
